Example of a ETL pipeline 

Raw File
   ↓
Read Data
   ↓
Validate
   ↓
Remove Bad Records
   ↓
Handle Nulls
   ↓
Standardize
   ↓
Join Lookup Tables
   ↓
Aggregate
   ↓
Add Audit Columns
   ↓
Write to Delta/Table


1. Extract
   Read data from source systems.

2. Validate
   Check schema, nulls, duplicates, and, business rules.

3. Remove Bad Records
   Eliminate unusable records.

4. Handle Nulls
   Replace or manage missing values.

5. Standardize
   Make formats consistent.

6. Join Lookup Tables
   Enrich data with additional business information.

7. Aggregate
   Create business metrics and summaries.

8. Add Audit Columns
   Track load dates and processing history.

9. Load
   Store trusted data into Delta tables, warehouses, or marts.